    "sha": "cfe6806b34578e8779de54839d2525b8c91cb329",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOC6Axt9oAKGNmZTY4MDZiMzQ1NzhlODc3OWRlNTQ4MzlkMjUyNWI4YzkxY2IzMjk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Sam Elliott",
        "email": "aelliott@qti.qualcomm.com",
        "date": "2025-11-20T01:48:30Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Sam Elliott",
        "email": "aelliott@qti.qualcomm.com",
        "date": "2025-11-20T01:52:45Z"
      },
      "message": "Vendor Symbols cannot always be LOCAL\n\nThe requirement for Vendor symbols to be `STB_LOCAL` was added to\nparallel the requirement that mapping symbols be local, and also\nresolved some issues with these symbols conflicting with user\ndefinitions (local symbols can have duplicate names).\n\nHowever, unlike mapping symbols, Vendor Symbols may appear in Dynamic\nSymbol Tables, because we may have dynamic vendor relocations. Dynamic\nsymbol tables conventionally only hold GLOBAL and WEAK definitions.\n\nThis does bring up the problem of how to deal with a dynamic symbol\nwhich has a name that matches a vendor symbol. This might become a QoI\ndecision for the linker whether to emit an error gracefully.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "ca307ed757208605a1d6f3d1d23d7311e01838de",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv-non-isa/riscv-elf-psabi-doc/git/trees/ca307ed757208605a1d6f3d1d23d7311e01838de"
